  "instance_name": "objectification_of_women",
  "label": "Objectification of Women",
  "description": "The phrase 'saying hoes mad' relies on the stereotype that women are primarily valued for their physical appearance or sexual availability, reducing them to objects ('hoes') that can be 'mad' (i.e., sexually desirable or provocative). This is a form of misogynistic objectification that is not depicted visually but is central to the meme's punchline and its problematic message.",
